#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:62
msgid ""
"XML Alto is supported natively: just upload the files as media to search "
"inside it."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:66
msgid ""
"The xml media-type should be a precise one: either \"application/alto+xml\" "
"or \"application/vnd.pdf2xml+xml\", not \"text/xml\" or \"application/xml\"."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:70
msgid ""
"New files are automatically managed, but you may need modules Bulk Edit or "
"Easy Admin to fix old ones, if any."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:74
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Badly formatted xml files may be fixed dynamically, but it will affect "
"performance. See %1$sreadme%2$s."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:86
msgid ""
"A new option allows to include media metadata in search, not only full text."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:90
msgid "A new option allows to fix bad xml and invalid utf-8 characters."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:97
msgid ""
"The module supports the tsv format for quicker search results. See module "
"Extract OCR."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:104
msgid ""
"The module allows to do an exact search when the input is wrapped with "
"double quotes. If wanted and if you use a tsv index, a reindexation with "
"ExtractOcr is needed."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:117
msgid ""
"The module now supports IIIF Content Search 2.0 at /iiif-search/{id}/search/"
"1 or /iiif-search/{id}/search/2. The existing endpoint /iiif-search/{id}/"
"search is kept as defaut."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:141
msgid ""
"The module now manages extraction of texts without the need of the module "
"Extract OCR. Furthermore, most of the use cases are now managed "
"automatically: digital objects, item without alto, with an alto multi-pages "
"or with alto by page, item without pdf or with a pdf or with multiple pdf by "
"page, various naming convention."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:162
msgid ""
"Settings \"iiifsearch_xml_image_match\" and \"iiifsearch_alto_page_match\" "
"have been removed. Pairing is now controlled by "
"\"iiifsearch_alto_pairing_mode\" (auto cascade by default). Multipage ALTO "
"page-to-canvas resolution is auto-detected (PHYSICAL_IMG_NR, Page ID "
"matching media basename, then positional)."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:168
msgid ""
"DigitalObjects attached to items via the configured properties (see the "
"DigitalObject module config) are now picked up by IIIF Search, the pairer "
"and the annotation/seeAlso endpoints alongside native medias."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:209
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d media attached to items use the legacy pdf2xml or tsv format. Attaching "
"those OCR derivatives is no longer recommended: the module stores them as "
"files under files/alto/ and files/iiif-search/. Do not remove them before "
"these files exist, since they may be the only source of the search: first "
"run the job Extract OCR in mode \"missing\" with the destination \"file\", "
"that requires the command-line utility pdftotext (package poppler-utils); "
"then use the bulk processing tab \"Cleanup module-created medias\". The "
"cleanup keeps the medias of the items without file. ALTO medias remain "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:224
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Setting \"iiifsearch_extract_types_media\" includes pdf2xml or tsv (%1$s). "
"These formats should be stored as flat files, not as medias. Move them to "
"\"iiifsearch_extract_types_files\" in the Extraction tab. ALTO may still be "
"attached as media if you wish."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:235
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Setting \"iiifsearch_extract_types_digital_object\" includes pdf2xml or tsv "
"(%1$s). These formats should be stored as flat files. Move them to "
"\"iiifsearch_extract_types_files\". ALTO may still be attached as a digital "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:252
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d digital objects use the legacy pdf2xml or tsv format. Attaching those "
"OCR derivatives is no longer recommended: the module stores them as files "
"under files/alto/ and files/iiif-search/. Do not remove them before these "
"files exist: first run the job Extract OCR in mode \"missing\" with the "
"destination \"file\", that requires pdftotext; then use the cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:297
msgid ""
"Extraction settings have been reorganised per format. Each format (TSV, by-"
"word TSV, ALTO, pdf2xml) now exposes its own list of destinations (file / "
"media / digital object). The recommended defaults are: file for TSV, by-word "
"TSV and ALTO; nothing for pdf2xml (deprecated). ALTO may additionally be "
"attached as media or digital object if you need it exposed as a regular "
"Omeka resource. TSV and pdf2xml should never be."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:336
msgid ""
"Canvas seeAlso/annotations are now controlled by three independent toggles "
"in the Text tab (ALTO, annotations, hOCR). ALTO and annotations are enabled "
"by default; hOCR is opt-in and requires a native hOCR media on the item."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:366
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Repaired the media type of %d text files that were wrongly detected as a "
"binary type (audio/video/image). Reindex the search and regenerate manifests "
"if needed."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:388
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Unable to write the file .htaccess in the directories %s: the ocr files may "
"be readable by anybody. Deny the access to them in the config of the server."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:393
msgid ""
"The direct web access to the directories of the ocr files is now denied: "
"these files are served only through the module, that checks rights."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:398
msgid ""
"The endpoints moved from /iiif-search/{id} to /iiif/search/{id}. The old "
"urls are redirected, but the manifests cached by the module IIIF Server "
"(directory files/iiif) should be cleared to use the new ones."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:402
msgid ""
"The table of contents of a tei file attached to an item is now extracted and "
"used as structures of the manifest by the module IIIF Server. It can be "
"stored in a property too (option \"Store the table of contents of the TEI "
"file in a property\")."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:410
msgid ""
"The invalid utf-8 characters and the malformed xml files are now repaired "
"automatically, only when needed, so the option to fix them was removed. Each "
"repaired file is logged, so it can be fixed."
msgstr ""

